WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.840
The third episode of Game of Thrones' eighth
season wasted no time diving into the action

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.320
of the Battle of Winterfell, coming in hot
and holding nothing back.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.200
Sure to be remembered as one of the most epic
entries in Thrones history, "The Long Night"

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.240
pitted the living against the dead, the light
against the dark, and fire against ice.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.920
Many characters took their final breaths in
the cold Winterfell air.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.480
Here's a look at the characters who didn't
make it, and one big winner.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.660
The bodies start falling from the first swing
of a sword.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:33.800
Even equipped with flaming weapons and steadfast
determination, the Dothraki aren't men of

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.720
myths or the enders of the Long Night.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.820
Soon after they forge ahead into the darkness,
with Jon's direwolf Ghost charging alongside

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.200
them, the Dothraki outriders are wiped out
by the wights.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.380
The side of the living quickly becomes overwhelmed
by the dead.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:52.200
Jon and Daenerys send their dragons, Rhaegal
and Drogon, out into battle to breathe fire

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.980
onto the enemy, to little avail.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.540
The dead aren't dying, an out-of-this-world
windstorm clouds everyone's vision, people

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.550
are dropping left and right, and the episode's
first major death comes when Lord Commander

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:07.280
of the Night's Watch Dolorous Edd dies via
stabbing when trying to save Samwell Tarly.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.720
Newly knighted Brienne then orders the forces
to retreat into Winterfell's gates.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.100
"Fall back!"

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.040
The speed at which the battle devolves into
chaos pushes Arya to send her sister Sansa

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.480
to the crypts, the so-called safest place
in Winterfell, with a dragonglass dagger.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.280
"I don't know how to use it."

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.740
"Stick them with the pointy end."

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.080
In the catacombs, Sansa joins her former husband
Tyrion Lannister, Sam's partner Gilly, Varys,

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.960
and Missandei, plus every woman, child, and
elderly person in Winterfell.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.520
Sansa, Tyrion, and Missandei exchange barbs
before the situation becomes no laughing matter.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:47.490
As fans predicted, the corpses resting in
the Stark family crypt come back to life and

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.480
take victims down with zero difficulty or
remorse.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.400
While dozens die screaming behind them, Sansa,
Tyrion, Gilly, Varys, and Missandei make it

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.200
out of the crypts alive, and their survival
may spell trouble moving forward.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.759
Tyrion, Varys, and Missandei are on Daenerys'
side; they've all bent the knee and pledged

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:05.520
loyalty to her.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.460
Sansa, on the other hand, hasn't warmed up
to her yet, and might never once she realizes

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.440
that Jon is the true heir to the Iron Throne.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.240
Theon Greyjoy has done some serious repenting
since betraying House Stark at the start of

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.560
the War of the Five Kings.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.720
Taken in as a ward and a prisoner of Ned Stark
following his own father's duplicity, Theon

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.580
grew up in Winterfell and had long been considered
a member of the Stark family.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:33.160
Theon's treachery against the Starks reached
its apex when he seized Winterfell in the

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.000
second season of Game of Thrones, capturing
two farm boys and displaying their burned

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.060
bodies on the castle's walls, passing them
off as Bran and Rickon Stark.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.720
Beneath the Weirwood tree in Winterfell's
godswood, where Bran awaits the Night King,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.480
Bran absolves Theon of his sins.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.180
Bran tells him that everything he's done brought
him to where he is now: home.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:57.880
You are a good man."

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.400
The Night King then emerges, and Theon attempts
stab him with a spear, but it's no use.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.860
The Night King kills Theon with a swift jab.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.280
There's a bright side, though: at least he
died knowing Sansa, Jon, and finally Bran

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.280
forgave him.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.180
Several more perished fighting in the Battle
of Winterfell.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.540
Beric Dondarrion was all out of extra lives
when the wights stabbed him multiple times

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.980
while he protected Arya.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.640
Little Lyanna Mormont, the ferocious lass
from Bear Island who insisted she take part

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:29.210
in the fight, dies a heroic death when she
bravely stabs a wight giant in the eye and

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.640
is subsequently crushed in its hand.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.620
Alys Karstark falls offscreen.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.300
She was among the people protecting Bran alongside
Theon in the godswood.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.760
Then came Jorah Mormont, who died defending
Daenerys to the bitter end.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.790
When a pack of wights unleash fury on Drogon,
who takes flight and abandons Dany, the Mother

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.460
of Dragons is left to fight off enemies herself
— until Jorah swoops in and protects her

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.420
from what end up being fatal blows.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.900
Dany sheds many tears over the loyal Jorah.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:01.500
As the sun begins to rise and the night slips
under the horizon, the Red Woman Melisandre

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.810
walks out of Winterfell, stepping between
two mounds of dead bodies like Moses parting

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.340
the Red Sea, and willingly ends her own life.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.100
She removes the red-amulet-adorned necklace
that perpetually sat around her throat, continues

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.260
out into the battlefield, and leaves this
mortal coil.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.320
In season 6, it was revealed that Melisandre
wasn't the youthful woman she appeared to

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:20.820
be.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.140
She was incredibly old, and the necklace extended
her life.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.600
With it off for too long, she was bound to
succumb to the effects of extreme old age.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.960
Melisandre likely felt her work in Westeros
was complete, and she may have been harboring

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.360
guilt over the death of little Shireen Baratheon,
whom she helped burn at the stake in season

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:37.860
5.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.680
She also kept good on two past promises.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.800
She once shared a prediction with Varys:

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.160
"I will return, dear spider.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:46.640
One last time."

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:47.540
"My lady…"

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.420
"I have to die in this strange country."

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.540
She also told Ser Davos at the start of the
Battle of Winterfell that she would "be dead

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.320
before dawn."

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.200
Arya didn't just evade death in the Battle
of Winterfell.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.140
She lengthed the lives of everyone in the
Seven Kingdoms by killing the Night King.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:07.080
In the corridors of Winterfell, Melisandre
reminds Arya that she will indeed "shut many

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.700
eyes forever … brown, green, and blue eyes,
too," a prophecy as to what Arya is about

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.200
to do.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.880
"What do we say to the god of death?"

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:20.940
"Not today."

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.979
Moments after the Night King sticks a spear
through Theon's torso and turns his attention

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:29.020
to Bran, Arya suddenly appears behind the
frosty villain.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.420
He attempts to choke her, and her Valyrian
steel dagger falls.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.000
But Arya catches the weapon with her other
hand, finds a space in the Night King's armor,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.419
and stabs him there, causing him and all of
his underlings to shatter into a million tiny

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:41.920
pieces.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:46.530
The Night King's undoing came around the same
place his "birth" did: in a godswood near

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.480
a Heart Tree.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:52.260
Even more poetically, Bran's life was saved
using the very same dagger that a catspaw

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.680
used during an attempt to assassinate him
way back in season one.

